1
00:00:01,809 --> 00:00:06,089
Chapter 38 Conclusion Reader.

2
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:08,029
I married him.

3
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:10,350
A quiet wedding we had.

4
00:00:11,169 --> 00:00:14,529
He and I, the passing and clerk, were alone present.

5
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:19,550
When we got back from church, I went into the kitchen of the manor house,

6
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:23,589
where Mary was cooking the dinner and John cleaning the knives, and I said,

7
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:30,309
Mary, I have been married to Mr. Rochester this morning.

8
00:00:31,589 --> 00:00:36,330
The housekeeper and her husband were both of that decent, fleagmatic order of

9
00:00:36,331 --> 00:00:42,250
people, to whom one may at any time safely communicate a remarkable piece of news,

10
00:00:42,869 --> 00:00:47,210
without incurring the danger of having one's ears pierced by some shrill

11
00:00:47,210 --> 00:00:53,149
ejaculation, and subsequently stunned by a torrent of wordy wonderment.

12
00:00:53,990 --> 00:01:00,850
Mary did look up, and she did stare at me, the ladle with which she was basting a

13
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:06,229
pair of chickens roasting at the fire, did for some three minutes hang suspended

14
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:10,353
in air, and for the same space of time, John's

15
00:01:10,354 --> 00:01:13,710
knives also had rest from the polishing process.

16
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:20,509
But Mary, bending again over the roast, said only, have you miss?

17
00:01:21,169 --> 00:01:22,169
Well for sure.

18
00:01:22,869 --> 00:01:24,270
A short time after she pursued.

19
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:27,614
I cede you go out with the master, but I didn't know

20
00:01:27,615 --> 00:01:31,529
you were gone to church to be wed, and she basted away.

21
00:01:32,270 --> 00:01:36,289
John, when I turned to him, was grinning from ear to ear.

22
00:01:37,369 --> 00:01:40,809
I told Mary how it would be, he said.

23
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:48,350
I knew what Mr. Edward, John was an old servant, and had known his master when he

24
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:52,990
was the cadet of the house, therefore he often gave him his Christian name.

25
00:01:54,229 --> 00:01:57,278
I knew what Mr. Edward would do, and I was certain

26
00:01:57,279 --> 00:02:00,610
he would not wait long neither, and he's done right.

27
00:02:01,029 --> 00:02:06,830
For ought I know, I wish you joy, miss, and he politely pulled his forelock.

28
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:08,970
Thank you, John.

29
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:12,470
Mr. Rochester told me to give you and marry this.

30
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:16,470
I put into his hand a five-pound note.

31
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:20,269
Without waiting to hear more, I left the kitchen,

32
00:02:20,270 --> 00:02:22,970
in passing the door of that sanctum sometime after.

33
00:02:23,729 --> 00:02:24,729
I caught the words.

34
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:28,729
She'll happen to better for him nor on ear to grand ladies.

35
00:02:29,589 --> 00:02:35,550
And again, if she bent one of the handsomest, she's no one foul and very

36
00:02:35,551 --> 00:02:41,290
good -natured, and ah, his eun, she's fair, beautiful, only body may see that.

37
00:02:41,869 --> 00:02:46,949
I wrote to Morehouse and to Cambridge immediately, to say what I had done,

38
00:02:47,669 --> 00:02:51,350
fully explaining also why I had thus acted.

39
00:02:52,770 --> 00:02:55,789
Diana and Mary approved the step unreservedly.

40
00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:00,369
Diana announced that she would just give me time to get over the honeymoon,

41
00:03:01,009 --> 00:03:04,070
and then she would come and see me.

42
00:03:05,009 --> 00:03:07,816
She had better not wait till then, Jane, said

43
00:03:07,816 --> 00:03:10,751
Mr. Rochester, when I read her letter to him.

44
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:13,130
If she does, she will be too late.

45
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:16,190
For our honeymoon will shine our life long.

46
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:20,050
Its beams will only fade over your grave or mine.

47
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:23,169
How singeon received the news?

48
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:24,830
I don't know.

49
00:03:25,350 --> 00:03:27,850
He never answered the letter in which I communicated it.

50
00:03:28,529 --> 00:03:33,830
Yet six months after he wrote to me, without, however, mentioning Mr.

51
00:03:33,929 --> 00:03:40,070
Rochester's name or alluding to my marriage, his letter was then calm and,

52
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:42,669
though very serious, kind.

53
00:03:43,529 --> 00:03:47,550
He has maintained a regular, though not frequent correspondence ever since.

54
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:51,952
He hopes I am happy, and trusts I am not of those who live

55
00:03:51,952 --> 00:03:55,990
without God in the world, and only mind earthly things.

56
00:03:57,009 --> 00:04:00,589
You have not quite forgotten little Adele, have you, reader?

57
00:04:01,610 --> 00:04:02,610
I had not.

58
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:06,751
I soon asked an obtained leave of Mr. Rochester to

59
00:04:06,752 --> 00:04:09,690
go and see her at the school where he had placed her.

60
00:04:10,509 --> 00:04:13,809
Her frantic joy at beholding me again moved me much.

61
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,289
She looked pale and thin.

62
00:04:17,289 --> 00:04:18,509
She said she was not happy.

63
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:22,789
I found the rules of the establishment were too strict.

64
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:26,970
It's a course of study too severe for a child of her age.

65
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:29,309
I took her home with me.

66
00:04:30,509 --> 00:04:35,710
I meant to become her governess once more, but I soon found this impracticable.

67
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:38,910
My time and cares were now required by another.

68
00:04:39,089 --> 00:04:41,449
My husband needed them all.

69
00:04:42,369 --> 00:04:48,869
So I sought out a school, conducted on a more indulgent system, and near enough to

70
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:53,089
permit of my visiting her often, and bringing her home sometimes.

71
00:04:53,809 --> 00:04:58,510
I took care she should never want for anything that could contribute to her comfort.

72
00:04:59,149 --> 00:05:03,437
She soon settled in her new abode, became very

73
00:05:03,438 --> 00:05:06,970
happy there, and made fair progress in her studies.

74
00:05:08,029 --> 00:05:13,589
As she grew up, a sound English education corrected in a great measure her French

75
00:05:13,591 --> 00:05:19,169
defects, and when she left school, I found in her a pleasing and obliging

76
00:05:19,171 --> 00:05:23,889
companion, docile, good tempered, and well principled.

77
00:05:24,729 --> 00:05:30,910
By her grateful attention to me and mine, she has long since well repaid any little

78
00:05:30,910 --> 00:05:34,250
kindness I ever had it in my power to offer her.

79
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:37,350
My tale draws to its close.

80
00:05:38,509 --> 00:05:44,009
One word respecting my experience of married life, and one brief glance at the

81
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:48,350
fortunes of those whose names have most frequently recurred in this narrative,

82
00:05:48,869 --> 00:05:50,210
and I have done.

83
00:05:51,449 --> 00:05:53,649
I have now been married ten years.

84
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:59,229
I know what it is to live entirely for and with what I love best on earth.

85
00:06:00,470 --> 00:06:02,690
I hold myself supremely blessed.

86
00:06:03,789 --> 00:06:06,830
Blessed beyond what language can express, because

87
00:06:06,831 --> 00:06:10,111
I am my husband's life as fully as he is mine.

88
00:06:10,970 --> 00:06:14,793
No woman was ever near to her mate than I am, evermore

89
00:06:14,794 --> 00:06:18,369
absolutely bone of his bone and flesh of his flesh.

90
00:06:19,169 --> 00:06:22,289
I know no weariness of my Edward society.

91
00:06:22,929 --> 00:06:26,605
He knows none of mine, any more than we each do of the

92
00:06:26,607 --> 00:06:29,970
pulsation of the heart that beats in our separate bosoms.

93
00:06:30,869 --> 00:06:32,789
Consequently, we are ever together.

94
00:06:33,809 --> 00:06:39,009
To be together is for us to be at once as free as in solitude, as gay as in company.

95
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:42,850
We talk, I believe, all day long.

96
00:06:43,649 --> 00:06:48,250
To talk to each other is but a more animated and an audible thinking.

97
00:06:49,149 --> 00:06:51,550
All my confidence is bestowed on him.

98
00:06:52,529 --> 00:06:54,610
All his confidence is devoted to me.

99
00:06:55,589 --> 00:06:58,050
We are precisely suited in character.

100
00:06:59,029 --> 00:07:01,009
Perfect concord is the result.

101
00:07:02,429 --> 00:07:05,990
Mr. Rochester continued blind the first two years of our union.

102
00:07:06,990 --> 00:07:12,089
Perhaps it was that circumstance that drew us so very near, that knit us so very

103
00:07:12,091 --> 00:07:17,029
close, for I was then his vision as I am still his right hand.

104
00:07:17,589 --> 00:07:22,789
Literally, I was, what he often called me, the apple of his eye.

105
00:07:23,570 --> 00:07:29,669
He saw nature, he saw books through me, and never did I weary of gazing for his

106
00:07:29,671 --> 00:07:35,429
behalf, and of putting into words the effect of field, tree, town, river,

107
00:07:35,669 --> 00:07:41,710
cloud, sunbeam, of the landscape before us, of the weather round us, and

108
00:07:41,710 --> 00:07:46,970
impressing by sound on his ear, what light could no longer stamp on his eye.

109
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:52,889
Never did I weary of reading to him, never did I weary of conducting him where

110
00:07:52,891 --> 00:07:57,350
he wished to go, of doing for him what he wished to be done.

111
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:04,389
And there was a pleasure in my services, most full, most exquisite, even though

112
00:08:04,391 --> 00:08:10,410
sad, because he claimed these services without painful shame or damping humiliation.

113
00:08:11,210 --> 00:08:17,009
He loved me so truly, that he knew no reluctance in profiting by my attendance.

114
00:08:17,869 --> 00:08:22,054
He felt I loved him so fondly, that to yield that

115
00:08:22,055 --> 00:08:25,630
attendance was to indulge my sweetest wishes.

116
00:08:26,570 --> 00:08:30,929
One morning, at the end of the two years, as I was writing a letter to his

117
00:08:30,930 --> 00:08:35,437
dictation, he came and bent over me and said, Jane,

118
00:08:35,437 --> 00:08:38,910
have you a glittering ornament round your neck?

119
00:08:39,250 --> 00:08:41,309
I had a gold watch chain, I answered yes.

120
00:08:42,710 --> 00:08:44,770
And have you a pale blue dress on?

121
00:08:45,589 --> 00:08:46,589
I had.

122
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:52,429
He informed me then, that for some time he had fancied the obscurity, clouding one

123
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:56,770
eye was becoming less dense, and that now he was sure of it.

124
00:08:58,169 --> 00:08:59,789
He and I went up to London.

125
00:09:00,949 --> 00:09:03,941
He had the advice of an eminent oculist, and he

126
00:09:03,941 --> 00:09:07,130
eventually recovered the sight of that one eye.

127
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:10,050
He cannot now see very distinctly.

128
00:09:10,830 --> 00:09:16,311
He cannot read or write much, but he can find his way without being led by the hand.

129
00:09:16,369 --> 00:09:20,449
The sky is no longer a blank to him, the earth no longer avoid.

130
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:27,089
When his first born was put into his arms, he could see that the boy had inherited

131
00:09:27,091 --> 00:09:31,449
his own eyes, as they once were, large brilliant and black.

132
00:09:32,449 --> 00:09:35,751
On that occasion, he again, with a full heart,

133
00:09:35,752 --> 00:09:39,389
acknowledged that God had tempered judgment with mercy.

134
00:09:40,729 --> 00:09:44,133
My Edward and I then are happy, and the more so,

135
00:09:44,134 --> 00:09:47,350
because those we most love are happy likewise.

136
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:53,429
Diana and Mary Rivers are both married, alternately, once every year.

137
00:09:53,869 --> 00:09:56,110
They come to see us, and we go to see them.

138
00:09:57,529 --> 00:10:02,630
Diana's husband is a captain in the Navy, a gallant officer and a good man.

139
00:10:03,750 --> 00:10:07,538
Mary's is a clergyman, a college friend of her brothers, and

140
00:10:07,539 --> 00:10:11,449
from his attainments and principles, worthy of the connection.

141
00:10:13,369 --> 00:10:19,389
Both Captain Fitz James and Mr. Wharton love their wives, and are loved by them.

142
00:10:20,669 --> 00:10:26,710
As to Syngin Rivers, he left England, he went to India, he entered on the path

143
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:29,750
he had marked for himself, he pursues it still.

144
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:35,990
A more resolute, indefatigable pioneer never brought amidst rocks and dangers.

145
00:10:36,789 --> 00:10:40,396
Firm, faithful and devoted, full of energy

146
00:10:40,398 --> 00:10:44,971
and zeal and truth, he labors for his race.

147
00:10:45,050 --> 00:10:47,309
He clears their painful way to improvement.

148
00:10:47,910 --> 00:10:53,410
He hues down like a giant, the prejudices of creed and cast that encumber it.

149
00:10:54,130 --> 00:11:00,389
He may be stern, he may be exacting, he may be ambitious yet, but his is the

150
00:11:00,391 --> 00:11:03,654
sternness of the warrior great heart, who guards

151
00:11:03,656 --> 00:11:06,589
his pilgrim convoy from the onslaught of Apollion.

152
00:11:07,509 --> 00:11:12,889
His is the exaction of the Apostle, who speaks but for Christ when he says,

153
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:15,903
whosoever will come after me, let him deny

154
00:11:15,903 --> 00:11:20,230
himself and take up his cross and follow me.

155
00:11:20,850 --> 00:11:26,649
His is the ambition of the High Master Spirit, which aims to fill a place in the

156
00:11:26,650 --> 00:11:33,210
first rank of those who are redeemed from the earth, who stand without fault before

157
00:11:33,210 --> 00:11:37,868
the throne of God, who share the last mighty victories

158
00:11:37,869 --> 00:11:43,610
of the Lamb, who are called and chosen and faithful.

159
00:11:45,229 --> 00:11:51,550
Sinjin is unmarried, he never will marry now, himself has hitherto suffice to the

160
00:11:51,551 --> 00:11:57,690
toil and the toil draws near its close, his glorious sun hastens to its setting.

161
00:11:58,990 --> 00:12:02,835
The last letter I received from him drew from my eyes

162
00:12:02,835 --> 00:12:06,250
human tears and yet filled my heart with divine joy.

163
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:11,649
He anticipated his sure reward, his incorruptible crown.

164
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:18,130
I know that a stranger's hand will write to me next, to say that the good and

165
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:21,710
faithful servant has been called at length into the joy of his Lord.

166
00:12:22,589 --> 00:12:23,910
And why weep for this?

167
00:12:24,929 --> 00:12:27,410
No fear of death will darken Sinjin's last hour.

168
00:12:27,910 --> 00:12:32,729
His mind will be unclouded, his heart will be undaunted, his hope will be sure,

169
00:12:33,190 --> 00:12:37,309
his faith steadfast, his own words are a pledge of this.

170
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:42,089
My master, he says, has forewarned me.

171
00:12:42,990 --> 00:12:48,690
Daily he announces more distinctly, surely I come quickly, and hourly I more

172
00:12:48,691 --> 00:12:53,589
eagerly respond, our men, even so come Lord Jesus.

173
00:12:56,970 --> 00:12:58,190
Thank you for listening.

174
00:12:58,789 --> 00:13:02,729
If you like our recordings consider liking this video and subscribing to our channel,

175
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:04,729
so you don't miss any more audiobooks.
